<title>USA: TVA 1,065 MW Ala. nuke shut for refueling.</title>
<headline>TVA 1,065 MW Ala. nuke shut for refueling.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tennessee Valley Authority's 1,065 megawatt (MW) Browns Ferry nuclear power unit 3 was shut over the weekend for scheduled refueling and maintenance, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Monday.</p>
<p>The unit was taken off line Feb 22, and was tentatively set to resume power near March 13, the NRC said in its daily plant status report.</p>
<p>The unit is located in Decatur, Ala.</p>
<p>The adjoining 1,065 MW Browns Ferry nuclear power unit 2 was operating at full power as of early Monday, the NRC said.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +1 212 859 1627))</p>
